# Checkpoint trailer — clause menu & authoring

On-demand reference. Read when composing a `<!-- ckpt` trailer (the trigger for *when* to emit one lives in CLAUDE.md `## Checkpoint trailer`).

> Copy to `.claude/refs/checkpoint.md` and delete this note. Lives in `refs/`, not `rules/`: a `rules/` file without frontmatter would load every session. Clause names are harvested by `dstoic:checkpoint`, `dstoic:save-context` and `ring` — rename them and those skills lose the signal.

## Format

`<!-- ckpt` + any of the clauses below (omit empties, one clause ≤~20 words, author don't quote) then `-->`.

## Clauses

- `decision:` choice + why
- `reasoning:` consequence DERIVED this turn (even w/ no decision)
- `learning:` non-obvious fact/gotcha found
- `pivot:` frame/scope that changed
- `rejected:` path + why
- `constraint:` hard rule in force
- `assumption:` unverified premise the work rests on
- `open:` unresolved fork
- `definition:` term=meaning
- `refs:` path→anchor/URL

## Rules

- Skip on clarifying/ack/pure-tool turns.
- Keep `<!-- ckpt` stable (`/checkpoint` greps it).
